  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work the body and hat first as they are the largest pieces. Use a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring-a75"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to start every piece."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cylinder, 7 cm diameter and 9 cm tall in blue or green dk yarn. Work both ends closed. Stuff firmly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Head"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "19-round sphere, 7 cm diameter. The gnome has no visible eyes under the hat brim; skip safety eyes if preferred. Stuff firmly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hat"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tall cone, 7 cm base and 12 cm in red dk yarn. Do not stuff. The hat sits over the top of the head and is sewn around its base."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Arms (make 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Capsule, 2.5 cm wide and 5 cm long. Stuff lightly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sew the head to the top of the body. Place the hat over the top two-thirds of the head and sew it in place around the brim. Sew the arms to either side of the upper body."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Beard"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cut lengths of white or cream yarn, each about 8 cm. Attach them using lark's head knots to the lower face of the head below the hat brim to form a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "yarn-beard-a75"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "yarn beard"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Trim to shape."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "invisible-decrease-a75"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "invisible decrease"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for all shaping. Weave in all ends. Add a small buckle or button to the hat brim if desired."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Materials needed"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Approximately 29 g in body colour dk yarn, 6 g red for the hat, small amount of white for the beard. Polyester stuffing. Tapestry needle."
          }
        ]
      }
